---
import WorksheetLayout from '../../../../layouts/WorksheetLayout.astro';
---
<WorksheetLayout
  title="Elements Explorer"
  lesson="/courses/mfedu-2026/the-four-elements/"
  intro="Line, color, shape, texture — the four levers every designer pulls. Explore each one, then aim them at your story."
>
  <h2>Line</h2>
  <p>Draw three kinds of lines below: one that feels <strong>calm</strong>, one that feels <strong>energetic</strong>, one that feels <strong>strong</strong>.</p>
  <div class="ws-box"></div>

  <h2>Color</h2>
  <p>What color do you associate with each word? Fill the swatch or write the color name.</p>
  <div class="ws-grid">
    <div>
      <p>Angry: <span class="ws-hint">______________</span></p>
      <p>Powerful: <span class="ws-hint">______________</span></p>
      <p>Shy: <span class="ws-hint">______________</span></p>
      <p>Happy: <span class="ws-hint">______________</span></p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p>Nature: <span class="ws-hint">______________</span></p>
      <p>Water: <span class="ws-hint">______________</span></p>
      <p>Rich: <span class="ws-hint">______________</span></p>
      <p>Sad: <span class="ws-hint">______________</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Shape</h2>
  <p>Sketch a silhouette (just the outline!) that says <strong>robot</strong>, and one that says <strong>royalty</strong>. No details allowed — shape only.</p>
  <div class="ws-box"></div>

  <h2>Texture</h2>
  <p>Tape or glue the edge of 3–4 fabric swatches here. Next to each, write two words for how it feels — and whether light would pass through it, bounce off it, or glow behind it.</p>
  <div class="ws-box ws-box--tall"></div>
  <p class="ws-hint">Texture is secretly a lighting decision: fabric is what turns a bare LED into a glow.</p>

  <h2>Aim them at your story</h2>
  <p>My cause is: <span class="ws-hint">_________________________________________</span></p>
  <p>The line / color / shape / texture choices that would tell it best:</p>
  <div class="ws-lines"><div></div><div></div><div></div></div>
</WorksheetLayout>
